  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving maternal and newborn health in Malga Woreda, SNNPR, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia remains one of the poorest countries in the world, and their levels of maternal and infant mortality and morbidity are also amongst the highest in the world. Only 10% of births take place in health facilities. Women will learn about how to keep themselves and their babies safe and healthy in participatory women&#x2019;s groups. It will strengthen the service quality in health posts and health centres. This will result in improved community care, care-seeking behaviour, and uptake of services.</narrative>
  </description>
